Z||000000||FieroFuker||11-13-2001||02:18 PM||||I gots my redGT 1985 2.8 up to about 90k and whenever I blow the trany or engine I'm going go for a upgrade in engine size.<P>I was thinkin <BR>1. low mile SC 3.8, <BR>2. series II 3.8 with 75-100 hp NOS shot<BR>3. 3.4 with NOS 75-100 shot.<P>I'm trying to get between high 12s and low 13s on 1/4 tracks<P>1. Do all of these engines bolt up without mods?<P>2.  Can these engines be built to handle high rpms? (I like revy engins) <P>3. even if I dont go for a new engine. is there good enough upgrade kits for the 2.8 that would boost the power to 150+ hp? I checked the fierostore.com and they have a kit (is that kit worth it?). <P>Cost isnt a issue... since I work on my own stuff (have lift torch etc.) and my friend owns a machineshop is right down the road! WooT!<P>Just for conversation I have a friend that is going to put a quad four in his 88fiero from a 89 GrandAm (its the kick ass 190 hp high output one    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ). He runs his GrandAm 1/4@15.3 pretty good for a stock 150k+ miler I think. Its funny to see a grand am beat those assholes that think they are hot stuff in their stock 80s trans ams and camaros.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by FieroFuker (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000001||sqoach||11-13-2001||02:38 PM||||You might want to talk to Travis (1FST2M6). He's running a 2.8 (beefed up a bit) with a 125 (I think) shot. His best time was like 12.9 at the strip.<BR>But, if money isn't an issue, I'm sure you could go with just about anything. I know the 3800 motors are not an easy bolt on. But the 3.4 bolts up pretty easily.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">               <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
